      "name": "an envelope of exactly the published limit is judged",
      "law": "The carriage",
      "obligations": ["III-6", "IX-5"],
      "derivation": "An ordinary ask whose whole envelope is exactly the number this door publishes as its `limit`. Article IX defines that number: \"the largest message it will accept, counted in bytes of the whole envelope as the carriage delivers it — the ephemeral key and the ciphertext together.\" Largest it will accept, so a message of exactly that size is accepted and judged like any other, and the answer is the estate this voice reaches. This is the half of the pair that a door erring one byte the other way would fail.",
